WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.390
Service path. Whose image is running.

2
00:00:09.258 --> 00:00:11.308
Which commit does each service run?

3
00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:18.170
At spi up, the CLI asks GHCR,
for each of thirteen forks,

4
00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:22.450
which digest main-snapshot names,
and records it in the image lock,

5
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:24.060
under the commit's sha tag.

6
00:00:26.342 --> 00:00:29.472
Partition's tag names a
commit on its fork's main,

7
00:00:29.502 --> 00:00:32.672
an upstream integration
merged that same day.

8
00:00:33.622 --> 00:00:39.302
On GHCR, that tag points at one
digest, and that digest is what both

9
00:00:39.302 --> 00:00:40.992
partition pods run.

10
00:00:41.942 --> 00:00:45.142
A tag can move. The lock keeps the digest,

11
00:00:45.142 --> 00:00:46.832
and the build date beside it.

12
00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:51.776
Whose image? The fork's, from
one commit you can read.

13
00:00:54.074 --> 00:00:56.564
Every image ages from
the day it was built:

14
00:00:56.794 --> 00:00:59.204
the Built column in spi info.

15
00:00:59.754 --> 00:01:03.044
Once it is old enough, and
main has built past it,

16
00:01:03.194 --> 00:01:06.074
GHCR retention can delete it.

17
00:01:06.074 --> 00:01:11.844
So spi info and spi status
mark an old canonical,

18
00:01:11.994 --> 00:01:13.524
and a refresh moves it.

19
00:01:15.718 --> 00:01:17.048
An easy mistake:

20
00:01:17.198 --> 00:01:20.568
my environment picks up the
fork's new main on its own.

21
00:01:20.878 --> 00:01:26.478
It doesn't. spi up chooses images once,
and running it again keeps the lock unless

22
00:01:26.478 --> 00:01:28.008
you ask for a refresh.

23
00:01:28.478 --> 00:01:31.608
Only the shared environment
refreshes on a schedule.

24
00:01:31.918 --> 00:01:35.438
On yours, read the built date in spi info,

25
00:01:35.438 --> 00:01:38.568
and refresh before the mark
becomes a deleted image.

26
00:01:41.178 --> 00:01:42.428
So now you can say:

27
00:01:42.658 --> 00:01:46.578
the lock ties each service to
one fork commit and one digest,

28
00:01:46.578 --> 00:01:48.668
and it moves only when I refresh it.

29
00:01:51.082 --> 00:01:54.852
Next: how do I prove a change
before a pull request?

